Subject: [PATCH] player: make FILL/CROP scale uniformly (cover) instead of stretching

"填充" (FILL) previously mapped to Modifier.fillMaxSize(), which forces the
video view to exactly the screen size. The video is drawn to fill the view,
so on displays that are not 16:9 the picture is stretched non-uniformly
(on a 3:2 screen a 16:9 video looks vertically stretched).

"裁剪" (CROP) was no better: it used fillMaxWidth + aspectRatio, i.e. the
width was locked to the screen width and the height came out shorter than
the screen, so the result was a *scaled-down* picture with letterbox bars,
visually identical to ORIGINAL.

Both branches are now: lock the height to the screen height, derive the width
from the real video ratio, and ask for height-first aspect ratio calculation.
The resulting view is wider than the screen, is centred, and gets cropped at
the sides - a uniform zoom ("cover").

Two things must both be right, and both are easy to get wrong:

  * Lsj7;->b is fillMaxHeight (Direction.Vertical) and Lsj7;->e is
    fillMaxWidth (Direction.Horizontal). Guessing them from the letters
    reproduces exactly the "scaled-down" bug described above.
  * Lpr;->p (matchHeightConstraintsFirst) must be true. With false the
    measurement tries width-first and returns 1080x607 on a 1080x720 screen.

Before:
    :cond_2b                                # ordinal 2 = CROP
        const/high16 v1, 0x3f800000         # 1.0f
        const/4 v5, 0x0                     # matchHeightConstraintsFirst = false
        invoke-static {v8, v1}, Lsj7;->e(Ld15;F)Ld15;   # fillMaxWidth(1.0f)  <-- wrong axis
        move-result-object v1
        iget-object v2, v6, Leu8;->e:Llm7;
        invoke-virtual {v2}, Llm7;->r()F
        move-result v2
        invoke-static {v1, v2, v5}, Lva0;->R(Ld15;FZ)Ld15;
        move-result-object v1
        goto :goto_1d

    :cond_2c                                # ordinal 1 = FILL
        invoke-static {v8, v1}, Lsj7;->c(Ld15;F)Ld15;   # fillMaxSize(1.0f) -> stretch

After (both branches become identical):
    :cond_2c                                # ordinal 1 = FILL
        const/high16 v1, 0x3f800000                     # 1.0f
        const/4 v5, 0x1                                 # matchHeightConstraintsFirst = true
        invoke-static {v8, v1}, Lsj7;->b(Ld15;F)Ld15;   # fillMaxHeight(1.0f)
        move-result-object v1
        iget-object v2, v6, Leu8;->e:Llm7;
        invoke-virtual {v2}, Llm7;->r()F                 # real video ratio
        move-result v2
        invoke-static {v1, v2, v5}, Lva0;->R(Ld15;FZ)Ld15;  # aspectRatio(ratio, true)
        move-result-object v1
        goto :goto_1d

Obfuscated Compose layout helpers in this build:

    Lmu1;->a = Direction.Vertical
    Lmu1;->b = Direction.Horizontal
    Lmu1;->c = Direction.Both

    Lsj7;->b  = fillMaxHeight      (FillElement, Vertical)
    Lsj7;->e  = fillMaxWidth       (FillElement, Horizontal)
    Lsj7;->c  = fillMaxSize        (FillElement, Both)
    Lva0;->R  = aspectRatio(ratio, matchHeightConstraintsFirst)
    Llm7;->r  = VideoPlayerState.aspectRatio
